# Model weights and binaries. Never commit these.
*.gguf
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.onnx
models/
tts/
bin/*.exe
bin/*.dll

# Runtime output
logs/
*.log
*.err
bench/results/*.json
bench/results/*.csv

# A dated file is a baseline and is kept. Everything else in results/ is
# scratch from a run someone was iterating on. Without this the numbers a
# decision was made on live only on one machine, which is where they die.
!bench/results/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.json

# The 28 August paired runs are raw local output. Their path-safe summary is in
# the documentation, so no file from that date is a public baseline.
bench/results/2026-08-28-*

# Recorded live sessions, which a bench result is not, so the dated exception
# above must not reach them. A proxy log holds the whole conversation: every
# tool call, every file the tools handed back, and the absolute paths they came
# from. The first one recorded here carried the path of a private working
# directory in six of its lines. A session log stays on the machine that
# recorded it, and the scored summary is what travels.
#
# Any depth, not just bench/results/. This used to name that one directory,
# while serve/README.md told the reader to run the recorder from the repository
# root and write session.jsonl there, which nothing ignored. The rule has to
# cover wherever the documented commands actually put the file.
*.jsonl

# These two files are constructed public fixtures, not recorded sessions.
# Name each exception so another JSONL dropped under samples/ stays ignored.
!samples/clean-account.jsonl
!samples/mismatched-account.jsonl

# Secrets and local overrides
.env
.env.*
config/local.*
*.key

# The template is the exception, and it has to be stated, because `.env.*`
# above matches it. Without this line the one file that documents the two
# variables the launchers need is invisible to git, and the omission looks
# exactly like having forgotten to write it.
!.env.example

# Editor and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Python bytecode, generated whenever a fixture test runs.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
